`armFor({ arm: null, set: null }, ['g2-deep-review-ask', 'cmd-x'])` to throw an error whose `code` is `mixed_row_arms`. Run `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and see it fail because `armFor` is not exported. Then in `R` make it `export function armFor(options, rowIds)`: an explicit `options.arm` wins, ids that are all `G2_ROWS` ids give `G2_SET`, ids that hold none give `DEFAULT_ARM` and a mix throws `new Refusal('mixed_row_arms', ...)` naming the started-command ids, with the comment saying a started-command row joins its own comparison whichever flag picked it. In `main`, change `options.arm = armFor(options);` to `options.arm = armFor(options, rowIds);`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node $PL/probe-arm-fixture.mjs` prints `--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm g2` and `--row-id g2-deep-review-ask --row-id cmd-x -> arm refused mixed_row_arms`.\n93: - [ ] T013 [P] Record the fixture on a g2 run line and replay it (`R`, `CO`, `BG`, `COT`). Test first: in `BG`, import `lineFixture` and expect `lineFixture({ fixture: '/custom/fixture' }, '/runs/arm/g2-fixture')` to be `'/custom/fixture'` and `lineFixture({}, '/runs/arm/g2-fixture')` and `lineFixture({ fixture: '' }, '/runs/arm/g2-fixture')` to be `'/runs/arm/g2-fixture'`. In `COT`, add `it('hands each line to the prompt lookup')`, whose `promptFor` records its second argument for a line carrying `fixture: '/custom/fixture'`, with `trusted: () => true` and stub warm, replay and brief, expecting the recorded line's `fixture` to be `'/custom/fixture'`. Run `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see both fail. Then in `CO` call `promptFor(row.rowId, row)` and say in its jsdoc that the lookup also receives the line. In `R` add `export function lineFixture(line, fallback)`, which returns `line.fixture` when it is a non-empty string and `fallback` otherwise, and in `backfillLog` pass